      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "If this were a traditional console game where the developers have complete control over all HUD elements, having a fixed HUD layout would be reasonable. However, in VRChat, many game worlds have designed their HUDs around the current HUD layout and positioning. If this design were implemented as-is, it could cause a wide range of issues, including compatibility problems with existing and older worlds.\n\nIf users were able to adjust the position of the HUD themselves, they would at least have a way to work around these issues on their end, making them much less likely to become critical problems.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2026-09-14T11:11:22.341Z",
  "deleteID": null,
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "This may just be my personal impression, but I felt my attention was focused on the center and lower parts of the screen, making it difficult to notice changes in the UI at the top.\n\nAlso, in many cases (such as FPS games), I think menu-style HUDs are located at the bottom of the screen.\n\nAs has already been pointed out in other Canny posts ( https://feedback.vrchat.com/open-beta/p/1916-mute-icon-has-a-bad-position-on-widescreen-monitors , https://feedback.vrchat.com/open-beta/p/1912-add-the-ability-to-move-and-resize-the-microphone-icon ), if we're playing VRChat in fullscreen mode or using a large monitor, having the UI displayed in a corner makes it hard to see, which isn't ideal.\n\nAt least, the HUD's position should be adjustable.\n\n(The attached images are rough mock-ups.)\n\nAlso, I think it's unlikely that a user seeing this UI (HUD) for the first time would think to press the Tab key to click on a HUD item. (I believe there are relatively few games with this kind of UI, and it isn't very intuitive.)\n\nTherefore, if the layout is designed on the assumption that users will click on HUD elements, I think it should be reconsidered.",
